From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:38:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Input: edt-ft5x06 - release contacts missing from a frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The controller lists every contact it tracks in every frame and reports
a lift once. The interrupt handler only ever released a slot on that
lift, so a contact the firmware stopped tracking without one stayed down
for good, and userspace saw a finger that never left. It was seen on an
FT3519T with the panel off, where it kept KWin's double tap to wake
from ever seeing a second tap.

Let the input core drop the slots a frame did not mention.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
index 0042361d1..9ccdce762 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
@@ -339,7 +339,12 @@ static irqreturn_t edt_ft5x06_ts_isr(int irq, void *dev_id)
 					       x, y, true);
 	}
 
-	input_mt_report_pointer_emulation(tsdata->input, true);
+	/*
+	 * The controller reports every contact in every frame, and a lift
+	 * only once. A contact that is gone without one, as happens when the
+	 * firmware gives up tracking it, would otherwise stay down for good.
+	 */
+	input_mt_sync_frame(tsdata->input);
 	input_sync(tsdata->input);
 
 out:
@@ -1325,7 +1330,7 @@ static int edt_ft5x06_ts_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	touchscreen_parse_properties(input, true, &tsdata->prop);
 
 	error = input_mt_init_slots(input, tsdata->max_support_points,
-				    INPUT_MT_DIRECT);
+				    INPUT_MT_DIRECT | INPUT_MT_DROP_UNUSED);
 	if (error) {
 		dev_err(&client->dev, "Unable to init MT slots.\n");
 		return error;
